      "id": "cpkc_te_safety_rule_book_april_2023_p004_b000",
      "title": "1",
      "text": "1\nPower Squats\nRepeat 15 consecutive power \nsquats. While keeping your \nhead and chest up, reach \nforward while sitting back \nkeeping your heels on the \nground and lower your legs \nas if you are about to sit \nback in a chair. Do not let \nyour knees go past 90° \nand keep your knees \nbehind your toes.\nAnti-slouch \nStretch\nAt the same time, bring your \nchin down and extend the \ncrown of your head up towards \nthe sky, gently contracting the \ncore to prevent arching of the \nback. Hold this position for 10 \nseconds, relax and repeat once.\n3\nThe daily stretches below are to be performed as  \na part of the Flex Stretch Prevent Program. You may \nperform additional stretches if you choose. Hold \nstretches for 5 – 10  seconds and continue to breathe \nthroughout, if you are holding your breath you \nhave gone too far. It is important to lightly engage \nyour core muscles at all times when stretching, do \nnot bounce or make any quick, jerky movements. \nStretching should be a slow and gentle movement \nwhere you may feel a mild discomfort but you \nshould not stretch to the point of pain. \nFLEX\nSTRETCH \nPREVENT\nStretches that should be completed \nbefore and during your work day.\nArm Circles\nKeeping palms facing up, do \n10 quick small circles forward \nand 10 backwards. Repeat \nwith 10 large circles forward \nand 10 large circles backwards. \nAs an option to increase \nmobility, add a shoulder shrug \nto your arm circles.\n2\nHamstring Stretch\nStep slightly forward with one \nleg placing the heel on the floor, \npointing the toe upward, causing \nthis leg to be straight. Bend the \nback knee, hinge at the hips, with \nyour back foot pointed forward; \nlead with the chest toward the \ntoes to keep the spine in neutral. If \nneeded the front heel can be placed \non a low step or you can hold onto \na steady object for support. Slowly \nprogress this stretch for 10 seconds, \nalternating twice on each side.\n5\n4\nReach Forward  \nand Across\nWhile keeping your back heel \non the ground and foot pointed \nforward, take a large step \nforward in a lunge position. \nYou may choose rest your hands \ngently on your front leg. Hold \nthis position for 10 seconds, \nalternate twice on each side.",
